#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:5
#: 141cc9d9a86d47ab9b832714a738edf3
msgid "Thrust Loss and Yaw Imbalance Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:7
#: 614f51a7247744d6ae21c2c10dc54d4e
msgid "If you see thrust loss or yaw imbalance warnings this page outlines some checks and modifications that should be done to resolve the issue. In the majority of cases these warnings are the result of incorrect hardware selection or setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:9
#: 23126d14089c4684be084e143f262bb6
msgid "These warnings are designed to detect hardware failures in the propulsion system. If they begin to occur on a vehicle that has been flying without warnings the propulsion system should be checked. Warnings are more likely to occur with larger payloads and in strong/gusty winds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:13
#: 9f850b03f7d2461181ccbf20ea5e575e
msgid "Potential Thrust Loss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:15
#: ff39cb01b233466eb40c3f57023cab91
msgid "If potential thrust loss messages are seen either on GCS or in the data-flash logs, then an investigation should be done to find the cause and remedy. The warning will give a motor number, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:17
#: d758159d98934f37955d5d244986ce44
msgid "```Potential Thrust Loss (3)```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:19
#: e669eb54bc42467386a4d97b02739f87
msgid "These warnings are the result of a motor or motors saturating at 100% throttle. Because of this saturation ArduCopter can no longer achieve the requested roll, pitch, yaw and throttle output. If this continues for a prolonged period of time the vehicle will have reduced altitude and attitude control and may crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:22
#: 2cd49cbf065f4753b7a386da19e1a9c1
msgid "If these messages are seen in hover or relaxed flight, the problem must be fixed in hardware. The vehicle's thrust to weight ratio should be increased, either by a change in propulsion or reduction in mass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:24
#: 63e479ee891d489a93afde289bc9ea72
msgid "If only seen in climbing and aggressive maneuvers it may be sufficient to lower the requested accelerations and speeds. Again the vehicle's thrust to weight ratio can be increased to allow higher accelerations and speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:29
#: 8c2d9b1481be4375b1c3d2384656bb2e
msgid "Yaw Imbalance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:31
#: 99cfd3c592894d2dae892a64ba4d268b
msgid "The yaw imbalance warning is a measure of how hard the vehicle is working to yaw, the warning will trigger before the yaw output is saturated. If the yaw output becomes saturated the vehicle's ability to maintain yaw will be compromised. And, in the worst case, this will result in the vehicle rapidly spinning. The warning message gives a percentage of maximum yaw output. At 100% it is saturated. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:34
#: 937eee317e8840289c4f49f0c9346db3
msgid "```Yaw Imbalance 87%```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:36
#: c2d0897889a64d64a4de88504debc48e
msgid "If seen in hover, the issue should be resolved in hardware. If the value is increasing with no pilot yaw input, the vehicle should be landed immediately. Yaw imbalance can be recognized in dataflash logs by comparing the PWM outputs between pars of opposing motors. It will present as a large throttle level difference between the clockwise and counter clockwise motors, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:42
#: c8a2bac8444548f693b8d5a76c2efb20
msgid "This should be fixed in hardware. The most common cause is the motors not being vertical on a circular arm. If the imbalance still persists the motors can be tilted slightly such that the thrust angle assists the yaw for its rotation direction. Some vehicles can be extremely sensitive to motors thrust vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:45
#: ff7edd4fa4ee4eb08673753a98238f34
msgid "If the warning is only seen in aggressive yaw maneuvers, the warning threshold can be increased by raising :ref:`ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX<ATC_RAT_YAW_IMAX__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`.  However, it may also be worth revisiting the yaw tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/thrust_loss_yaw_imbalance.rst:48
#: bb1d0bc847b343f0883bf2a7880240a0
msgid "Both the thrust loss and yaw imbalance warnings can be disabled with the :ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` parameter. This should only be done after extensive log review and testing to verify the warnings are not picking up genuine issues."
msgstr ""
